sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client (requests)
    participant G as Gateway / proxy
    participant S as Backend
    Note over C,S: A. Client timeout: the client gives up
    C->>G: GET /reports/slow (timeout=(3.05, 1))
    G->>S: forward
    Note over C,G: 1 s, no bytes → ReadTimeout<br/>(an exception, not a status code)
    Note over C,S: B. Gateway timeout: the gateway gives up
    C->>G: GET /reports/gateway
    G->>S: forward
    Note over G,S: upstream silent for 30 s
    G-->>C: 504 Gateway Timeout
    Note over C,S: C. Long job done asynchronously: nobody waits
    C->>S: POST /reports
    S-->>C: 202 Accepted · Location: /api/v1/jobs/1
    loop poll until complete
        C->>S: GET /jobs/1
        S-->>C: 200 {"status": "running"} · Retry-After: 1
    end
    C->>S: GET /jobs/1
    S-->>C: 200 {"status": "complete"}
